.TH OMORFOSCTL 1 "" omorfos "omorfos manual"
.nh
.ad l
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
omorfosctl \- Control a running omorfos compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBomorfosctl [\-\-socket PATH] <COMMAND>\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
It exits with 0 on success, 1 on failure or if \fBconfig check\fR found problems, and 2 for a usage error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Print the running compositor's version
.TP
\fBstate\fR
Print workspaces, windows and problems as JSON
.TP
\fBscreens\fR
Print the screens, where they stand and their modes
.TP
\fBframes\fR
Print how long each screen's last frame took to draw
.TP
\fBwatch\fR
Print the state, one JSON line each time it changes
.TP
\fBaction NAME [ARG]...\fR
Perform an action, as named in keys.yaml; \fBaction\fR alone lists them
.TP
\fBactivate ID\fR
Switch to a window, by the id shown in \fBstate\fR
.TP
\fBconfig check\fR
Print configuration problems; fails if there are any
.TP
\fBconfig reload\fR
Re\-read the configuration, then check it
.TP
\fBreport [\-\-whole]\fR
Print what a report of a fault needs, for you to look over before handing it on: versions, graphics cards, screens, state, configuration and the session's logs. Window titles and paths in your home are left out unless \-\-whole is given. Works without a running compositor
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-socket PATH\fR
The compositor's socket [default: $OMORFOS_SOCKET, or omorfos\-$WAYLAND_DISPLAY.sock in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR]
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print this help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print the version
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
omorfosctl action close
omorfosctl action workspace 2
omorfosctl action spawn foot \-\-title scratch
omorfosctl report > omorfos\-report.txt
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBomorfos\fR(1), \fBomorfos\-config\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-keys\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-rules\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-menu\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-theme\fR(5)
